Subject: [PATCH] test(cli): ACP model pin fails loud instead of falling back
 (red first)

Test-only commit for fork patch 0005. A pinned model (CLINE_MODEL at
session/new, session/set_config_option model, session/set_model) is kept when
the provider can route it and rejected with invalidParams naming the id
otherwise; the provider default (minimax.minimax-m2.5 on Bedrock) is used only
when nothing is pinned.

- Bedrock keeps aws-mantle/ ids and inference-profile ARNs outside the catalog.
- The unroutable id "aws-mantle/" (criteria k2.unroutableId) is rejected at
  session/new, set_config_option and set_model; a rejected change keeps the
  current model.
- A closed-catalog provider rejects an unknown id.

Rebased onto cli-v3.0.71 (test files taken from the rebased fork patch 0004, old number 0005).
